WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:06.310
The slow-burn monstrous horror of Midnight
Mass and its chilling story of angels, demons,

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:10.440
guilt and redemption, leads to an explosive
ending that will leave you thinking about

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:12.150
the show long after it's finished.

00:00:12.150 --> 00:00:16.570
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, I'm Jan and in
this video I'm explaining everything about

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:20.560
the ending of Midnight Mass, some crucial
details you might have missed, and why that

00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:23.710
final scene doesn't quite mean what you think
it does.

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.359
Obviously, spoilers ahead, so take care.

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:31.029
To fully understand the fiery finale, we need
to go back to the origin of the miracles and

00:00:31.029 --> 00:00:34.300
mysteries that occur on Crockett Island after
Father Paul arrives.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:38.790
Paul, as we discover in the third episode,
is actually the island's original priest,

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:43.400
the elderly Monsignor John Pruitt who's been
transformed into his younger self after a

00:00:43.400 --> 00:00:45.220
pilgrimage to Jerusalem.

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:50.070
During his trip, one day Pruitt was separated
from his group and ended up outside the city,

00:00:50.070 --> 00:00:51.740
wandering on the road to Damascus.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:56.300
As a sandstorm hit, he sought shelter in a
cave where he was attacked by a winged vampire

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:59.410
who bit his neck and began to consume his
blood.

00:00:59.410 --> 00:01:03.640
Before the priest died though, the creature
pierced its own skin and fed his blood to

00:01:03.640 --> 00:01:04.640
Pruitt.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:09.329
This is my blood..
..shed for you and for all so that sins may

00:01:09.329 --> 00:01:10.329
be forgiven.

00:01:10.329 --> 00:01:14.360
These words are from The Last Supper and are
a crucial part of the Catholic Mass and doctrine

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:18.840
which states that the bread and wine offered
during communion become the actual body and

00:01:18.840 --> 00:01:20.179
blood of Christ.

00:01:20.179 --> 00:01:24.509
By saying this about Pruitt receiving the
creature's blood, Paul shows that he believes

00:01:24.509 --> 00:01:28.210
it's a holy sacrament equivalent to the blood
of Christ.

00:01:28.210 --> 00:01:32.820
Pruitt believed it was an angel – notice
the Halo which he sees form around its head.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:36.920
Paul calls the wound the creature makes on
its wrist a stigmata, referencing the wounds

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:39.700
inflicted on Jesus when he was crucified.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:44.619
Also notice that the wood carvings illustrating
Pruitt's experience are numbered from 1 to

00:01:44.619 --> 00:01:49.890
14 in Roman numerals, a nod to the Stations
of the Cross, images often found in churches

00:01:49.890 --> 00:01:53.539
which depict the events of Jesus's crucifixion
and death.

00:01:53.539 --> 00:01:58.140
When Pruitt awakened he decided to take the
name Paul, in reference to Saul who became

00:01:58.140 --> 00:02:02.750
Paul when he experienced a life-changing event
on the road from Jerusalem to Damascus that

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:06.399
converted him to one of Christianity's most
renowned apostles.

00:02:06.399 --> 00:02:10.759
Similar to Saul, Father Paul believes it's
his duty to spread the miracle of what happened

00:02:10.759 --> 00:02:15.290
to him to the whole world and he begins by
smuggling the vampire back to Crockett Island

00:02:15.290 --> 00:02:16.370
in a trunk.

00:02:16.370 --> 00:02:21.099
On the island, Paul begins to add the creature's
blood to the communion wine, and little by

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:25.650
little those who take communion find their
physical ailments slipping away.

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:29.680
Riley's mother no longer needs glasses and
his father's back gets better.

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:34.239
Even more miraculously, the paralysed Leeza
finds she can now walk, while Sarah Gunning's

00:02:34.239 --> 00:02:38.319
mother Mildred regains her mental faculties
and begins to de-age incredibly.

00:02:38.319 --> 00:02:44.959
After a while on the island, Paul starts to
feel sick, then suddenly keels over and dies.

00:02:44.959 --> 00:02:50.290
A few minutes later, he comes back to life;
however, he now discovers that sunlight burns

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:51.290
his skin.

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:56.610
He's also no longer interested in regular
food, his body instead craving human blood,

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:00.519
which leads to Joe Collie's death and and
Paul's next bloody meal.

00:03:00.519 --> 00:03:05.420
Later, Paul discusses with Riley whether he
felt any remorse for his part in Joe's death

00:03:05.420 --> 00:03:10.140
and justifies his lack of guilt by quoting
something Beverley showed him in the Bible.

00:03:10.140 --> 00:03:12.930
The graces of the Holy Spirit rained down
on me..

00:03:12.930 --> 00:03:16.330
..cleansed my conscience, for I had simply
done His will.

00:03:16.330 --> 00:03:21.959
The priest's appeal to the Bible as justification
for his actions shows how misguided he's become

00:03:21.959 --> 00:03:26.760
and is a warning about those who use religion
as a reason to justify terrible behaviour

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:27.810
and atrocities.

00:03:27.810 --> 00:03:32.860
By contrast, Riley demonstrates the ability
to avoid giving in to temptation when he goes

00:03:32.860 --> 00:03:34.709
out on the boat with Erin.

00:03:34.709 --> 00:03:39.490
Riley's resistance here matches his own struggle
with alcohol addiction and how he genuinely

00:03:39.490 --> 00:03:44.349
felt culpable and remorseful and took responsibility
for the death of the girl he killed in the

00:03:44.349 --> 00:03:45.349
car accident.

00:03:45.349 --> 00:03:46.900
You struggled..
..with what happened

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:48.270
With what I did.

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:53.349
Paul however twists his religion to suit his
own purposes while making out that he's somehow

00:03:53.349 --> 00:03:56.680
doing God's will;
and together with the wickedly holier-than-thou

00:03:56.680 --> 00:04:01.630
Beverley Keane, puts into action a terrible
final plan for the Easter Vigil.

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:06.670
At the Midnight Mass, Beverley distributes
cups with a lethal poison while Paul urges

00:04:06.670 --> 00:04:09.470
everyone to drink so they can die and be reborn.

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:15.010
Let your earthly body die, so that your divine
body can awaken.

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:18.829
Anyone who's already taken communion since
Paul's arrival on the island will have drunk

00:04:18.829 --> 00:04:23.000
some of the Angel's blood and so they will
resurrect soon after dying.

00:04:23.000 --> 00:04:27.900
In the chaotic events that follow, the reborn
vampires attack any still-living humans as

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:29.680
they try to flee the church.

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:34.880
The events of the vigil bring to mind the
real-world Jonestown Massacre in 1978 when

00:04:34.880 --> 00:04:39.780
members of the Peoples Temple cult committed
mass suicide after their leader Jim Jones

00:04:39.780 --> 00:04:44.080
exhorted everyone to drink a poison-laced
Kool-Aid-like drink.

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:48.710
The bloodbath at the church spills out onto
the rest of the island with Bev encouraging

00:04:48.710 --> 00:04:52.710
the new-born vampires to kill or convert anyone
left.

00:04:52.710 --> 00:04:57.419
She orders every building to be burned so
there'll be no refuge come sunrise except

00:04:57.419 --> 00:05:02.610
for the church and rec centre, and she sets
herself up as the moral arbiter of who's worthy

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:05.710
to be allowed in and who should perish in
the sunlight.

00:05:05.710 --> 00:05:10.581
By this point, Paul has reunited with Mildred
who's been reborn after being killed by the

00:05:10.581 --> 00:05:13.340
Angel,
and he confesses that his real reason for

00:05:13.340 --> 00:05:18.199
bringing the Angel to the island was selfish
as he wanted a second chance at life with

00:05:18.199 --> 00:05:20.020
Mildred and their daughter Sarah.

00:05:20.020 --> 00:05:25.169
Millie understands but counters that his wish
goes against the natural order of things.

00:05:25.169 --> 00:05:26.630
We lived our lives.

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:31.220
She grew up and we faded away, and that's
how it's supposed to work.

00:05:31.220 --> 00:05:36.229
The cost of his choice is stark as not only
have the vampire mob run riot over the island,

00:05:36.229 --> 00:05:40.900
but when Paul finds his daughter in the church
about to burn it down, she's suddenly shot

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:42.169
by Sturge.

00:05:42.169 --> 00:05:46.770
Paul tries to bring her back with his blood
before she dies but she spits it out rejecting

00:05:46.770 --> 00:05:49.470
the cursed resurrection that would come with
it.

00:05:49.470 --> 00:05:54.960
Paul fully understands the horror of the unnatural
force he unleashed and with Millie burns down

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:56.120
the church.

00:05:56.120 --> 00:06:00.710
The rec centre goes up in flames next thanks
to Sherriff Hassan and Erin who've doused

00:06:00.710 --> 00:06:04.509
it with petrol and, significantly, it's Ali
who sets it alight,

00:06:04.509 --> 00:06:08.650
as like Ed and Annie Flynn and some of the
others who turned into vampires, he's able

00:06:08.650 --> 00:06:13.830
to resist the urges that come with it and
he does what he can to stop the ghoulish enterprise

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:16.050
even if it means his own death.

00:06:16.050 --> 00:06:21.150
Erin in the meantime is attacked by the Angel,
but as it feeds on her she steadily slices

00:06:21.150 --> 00:06:26.110
the creature's wings tearing large holes into
them so it can no longer fly properly,

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:30.790
with the hope that it won't be able to reach
the mainland 30 miles away before sunrise.

00:06:30.790 --> 00:06:35.300
This moment was foreshadowed during her talk
with Riley about how, when Erin was a child,

00:06:35.300 --> 00:06:39.760
her mother wanted to clip the wings of a pair
of pet doves so they wouldn't fly away.

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:42.060
She said,
"Everyone gets their wings clipped at some

00:06:42.060 --> 00:06:43.060
point."

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:47.370
With the Rec centre burning, everyone apart
from Bev Keane accepts the fate that awaits

00:06:47.370 --> 00:06:51.690
them, and Sturge owns up to the horrors he's
participated in and asks for forgiveness.

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:53.470
Will you forgive me, kid?

00:06:53.470 --> 00:06:54.539
I'll forgive you.

00:06:54.539 --> 00:06:58.360
Paul asks Millie for forgiveness and tosses
his priest's collar away;

00:06:58.360 --> 00:07:02.599
and, as the remaining islanders await the
dawn, they sing the hymn "Nearer, My God,

00:07:02.599 --> 00:07:07.300
to Thee", a song often associated with funerals
and which some have said was played on The

00:07:07.300 --> 00:07:09.020
Titanic as it sunk.

00:07:09.020 --> 00:07:14.220
Hassan and Ali also pray on the beach until
Hassan's overcome by his wounds and his son

00:07:14.220 --> 00:07:15.390
burns up.

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:20.220
Bev Keane refuses to give in right to the
bitter end as she tries to dig a shelter in

00:07:20.220 --> 00:07:23.610
the sand before going up in flames like everyone
else.

00:07:23.610 --> 00:07:28.610
It's ironic that her second and final death
is burning to a crisp given how she decided

00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:32.949
to burn down the island and what she quoted
from the book of Revelation about how true

00:07:32.949 --> 00:07:35.590
sinners would die:
"As for the cowardly..

00:07:35.590 --> 00:07:39.919
..and all of the liars, their place will be
in the lake that burns..

00:07:39.919 --> 00:07:41.419
..which is the second death."

00:07:41.419 --> 00:07:46.800
Bev, of course, was a huge hypocrite and coward;
notice how at the Easter Vigil she didn't

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:51.599
drink the poison herself and hid in the back
of the building as the others became vampires.

00:07:51.599 --> 00:07:55.860
Unlike the rest of the islanders who find
solace together in their final moments, she's

00:07:55.860 --> 00:08:00.860
unable to accept responsibility for what's
to come and dies screaming in anger.

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:05.720
The only two people left alive by the end
are Leeza and Warren, Riley's younger brother.

00:08:05.720 --> 00:08:10.180
They escaped the massacre at the church without
dying and being resurrected as vampires, so

00:08:10.180 --> 00:08:12.389
they're able to survive the sunrise.

00:08:12.389 --> 00:08:17.220
The very last words of the finale are Leeza
saying she can no longer feel her legs, meaning

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:21.360
the healing effect of the Angel blood has
worn off and she's paralyzed again.

00:08:21.360 --> 00:08:25.470
Now, initially I assumed this implied the
Angel had died in the sunrise;

00:08:25.470 --> 00:08:29.930
however, in an interview with The Wrap, the
show's creator Mike Flanagan has said that's

00:08:29.930 --> 00:08:34.750
not exactly the case, although he seems to
acknowledge that it might be a valid interpretation

00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:35.959
of the ending.

00:08:35.959 --> 00:08:39.230
Flanagan said the reason Leeza was becoming
paralysed again was because:

00:08:39.230 --> 00:08:42.209
the "concentration in her blood had begun
to tip back.."

00:08:42.209 --> 00:08:45.930
and that they "didn't want it to confirm about
The Angel, in […] that you can never kill

00:08:45.930 --> 00:08:48.800
fanaticism, it'll always kind of come back."

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:53.870
What Flanagan is referring to about the concentration
in Leeza's blood tipping back is the scientific

00:08:53.870 --> 00:08:57.930
explanation that the island's doctor, Sarah
Gunning, came up with for what was going on

00:08:57.930 --> 00:09:00.079
with the blood tests she carried out.

00:09:00.079 --> 00:09:04.440
Sarah discovered that Erin and her mother's
blood only had relatively small amounts of

00:09:04.440 --> 00:09:08.940
an active substance which she saw burn up
whenever it was exposed to sunlight.

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:13.040
And she hypothesised that if the amounts of
this substance were small enough in a person's

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:17.600
body and they stopped receiving any more of
it, they would eventually excrete it from

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:18.600
their system.

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:23.760
I think when we ingest poison, alcohol, whatever,
before a certain point, if we stop taking

00:09:23.760 --> 00:09:26.390
it in, maybe our body can push it back out.

00:09:26.390 --> 00:09:30.500
This appears to be what happened with Leeza
as now that she's gone some time without communion,

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:34.860
the effects of the Angel blood seem to be
wearing off hence the return of her paralysis.

00:09:34.860 --> 00:09:39.360
By the way, if you want to know why Father
Paul was able to wander around in the daylight

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:43.390
for the first two episodes without burning
up, it's because he never actually died in

00:09:43.390 --> 00:09:44.390
the cave.

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:48.500
The Angel gave him blood to heal his wounds
while he was still alive, and because he hadn't

00:09:48.500 --> 00:09:53.180
died at that point and been reborn, he was
able to move around in the daylight.

00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:57.320
According to Flanagan, this was part of the
Angel's plan so that Paul could help the creature

00:09:57.320 --> 00:09:58.630
get out of the cave.

00:09:58.630 --> 00:10:03.200
Flanagan also said that the reason for Paul's
death in the third episode was because he'd

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:08.200
"taken in too much of the blood, [and it hit]
that critical mass that Sarah talks about".

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:12.470
What I think Flanagan's referring to is Sarah's
explanation that the Angel's blood is like

00:10:12.470 --> 00:10:17.700
a virus, a parasite or a poison of sorts and
that if it accumulates too much it can kill

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:18.700
you.

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:22.950
As a Catholic priest, Paul would be obliged
to consume all the leftover communion wine

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:27.260
from every Mass, so he'd likely be drinking
more of it than anyone else.

00:10:27.260 --> 00:10:32.170
Of course, Flanagan's suggestion that the
Angel isn't necessarily dead leaves the potential

00:10:32.170 --> 00:10:36.810
for a follow-up second season if we assume
that it did reach the mainland and find cover

00:10:36.810 --> 00:10:38.140
before the dawn.

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:42.670
As bad as those cuts were, the Angel does
have the power of self-healing, so although

00:10:42.670 --> 00:10:47.529
it's a horrifying thought, it does leave the
opportunity to pick up this story again should

00:10:47.529 --> 00:10:48.870
Flanagan want to.

